<title>USA: List of firms sued Thursday by Orange County.</title>
<headline>List of firms sued Thursday by Orange County.</headline>
<dateline>SANTA ANA, Calif. 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>California's Orange County on Thursday sued 21 firms and entities in seven complaints for their alleged involvement in the county's bankruptcy, the largest municipal bankruptcy in U.S. history. Among the companies targeted in the suit:</p>
<p>In its first complaint, the county sued:</p>
<p>- Bear Stearns &amp; Co Inc</p>
<p>- CS First Boston, a unit of CS Holding</p>
<p>- Dean Witter Reynolds Inc</p>
<p>- Nomura Securities International  </p>
<p>- Lehman Brothers</p>
<p>- Smith Barney Inc</p>
<p>- Donaldson Lufkin &amp; Jenrette Inc</p>
<p>- Prudential Bache Securities</p>
<p>- PaineWebber Inc</p>
<p>- Daiwa Securities (America) Inc</p>
<p>- Cantor Fitzgerald</p>
<p>- Citicorp Securities Inc</p>
<p>- Kidder Peabody &amp; Co</p>
<p>- Sanwa Securities Co (USA)</p>
<p>- SBC Capital Markets Inc, a unit of Swiss Bank Corp</p>
<p>In its second through seventh complaints, the county sued:</p>
<p>- BA Securities, a unit of BankAmerica Corp</p>
<p>- Paribas Corp</p>
<p>- Brown &amp; Wood</p>
<p>- Federal National Mortgage Association</p>
<p>- Federal Home Loan Banks</p>
<p>- Federal Farm Credit Banks</p>
</text>
